      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Carbon-ceramic pads typically exhibit lower thermal conductivity and a more gradual temperature increase during braking compared to semi-metallic pads. This is due to the ceramic material's higher thermal insulation properties and slower heat transfer. As a result, carbon-ceramic pads tend to maintain rotor surface temperatures at lower levels, which can lead to reduced wear and improved braking performance.",
